        "plan": {
          "files": [
            "quantity.mjs"
          ],
          "change": "Create quantity.mjs at repo root as an ES module. Read all of stdin, trim it, then parse with `const n = parseInt(input, 10);` and check `Number.isInteger(n) && n > 0`. If true, print JSON.stringify({quantity: n}) to stdout; otherwise print JSON.stringify({error: \"invalid_quantity\"}). This is the first candidate implementation, using parseInt on the trimmed input to accept positive integers.",
